  "name": "geneva-montblanc",
  "notes": "Lake Geneva basin to the Mont Blanc massif for an IKEA SANNAHED 50 x 50 cm box frame (6 cm deep). The frame's visible window is a little under 50 cm (about 47.4 cm scaled off IKEA's drawing), so the relief is 47.5 x 47.5 cm (user decision 2026-11-05): 2x2 tiles of 237.5 mm at 1:200,000 = 47.5 km per tile. Projected on ETRS89 / UTM zone 32N (EPSG:25832), the European reference grid, so the overlay's 10 km grid (MGRS square letters) is straight. Bands: water, two vegetation tiers, rock, snow. No shore band (dropped 2026-09-28). 5 colours on 4 slots: palette.overflow='swap' plans one manual swap (lowland -> snow) on the Mont Blanc tile. Exaggeration fixed at 2.0x (tallest tile ~49 mm, fits the 6 cm frame). Filaments (2026-11-05, user's spools): slot 1 glossy blue (water+base), 2 matte army dark green (lowland), 3 matte grey (rock), 4 matte wood brown (upland); white swapped into slot 2 for snow.",
